{"blocks":[["Audio/Connector/Phone/","source-block-1731","TRRS Wiring Standards",["Phone Connector (audio)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/","source-block-1759","TRRS adds a mic/ground ring, but two incompatible wiring orders exist:",["Phone Connector (audio)","TRRS Wiring Standards"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/","source-block-1834","CTIA/AHJ (Apple, most modern Android/Windows devices): tip = left, ring 1 = right, ring 2 = ground, sleeve = mic",["Phone Connector (audio)","TRRS Wiring Standards","TRRS adds a mic/ground ring, but two incompatible wiring orders exist:"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/","source-block-1956","OMTP (older Nokia and some Asian-market phones): tip = left, ring 1 = right, ring 2 = mic, sleeve = ground",["Phone Connector (audio)","TRRS Wiring Standards","TRRS adds a mic/ground ring, but two incompatible wiring orders exist:"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/","source-block-2072","Plugging a headset wired to one standard into a jack wired to the other leaves left/right audio unaffected but the microphone silent, since only the mic/ground pair is swapped",["Phone Connector (audio)","TRRS Wiring Standards"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/","source-block-60","TRRS — Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve",[]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/","source-block-94","Four contacts, three insulating rings. Adds a microphone and inline-remote contact to the stereo pair of Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS.",["TRRS — Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/","source-block-233","Two wiring orders are in circulation, CTIA/AHJ and OMTP. Both put left on the tip and right on the first ring, and they swap the microphone and ground between the second ring and the sleeve.",["TRRS — Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/","source-block-427","Five-contact successors exist: TRRRS at 3.5 mm under ITU-T P.382, adding a second microphone or a power line, and the 4.4 mm Pentaconn under JEITA RC-8141C for balanced headphone cable.",["TRRS — Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/","source-block-616","Sizes",["TRRS — Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/","source-block-628","Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm — phone and tablet headsets. Defined by JEITA/EIAJ RC-5325A.",["TRRS — Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve","Sizes"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-148","3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector",[]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-194","Visual Reference",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-368","Image: public domain (CC0), via Wikimedia Commons",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Visual Reference"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-496","Overview",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-511","TRRS stands for Tip-Ring-Ring-Sleeve: 4 conductors, 3 insulating rings",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Overview"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-590","Extends Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm with a second ring, used to carry a microphone signal and/or inline remote-control signal (play/pause, volume, call answer)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Overview"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-762","Standard connector for phone/tablet headsets that combine stereo output with a microphone",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Overview"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-856","Physical Specifications",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-886","Diameter: 3.5 mm (1/8 in)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-920","Conductors: 4 (tip, ring, ring, sleeve)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-968","Insulating rings: 3",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-996","Orientation: rotationally symmetric, no keying",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1051","Pin Configuration — CTIA/AHJ (modern standard)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1106","Tip: left channel",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — CTIA/AHJ (modern standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1132","Ring 1: right channel",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — CTIA/AHJ (modern standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1162","Ring 2: ground",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — CTIA/AHJ (modern standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1185","Sleeve: microphone / inline remote",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — CTIA/AHJ (modern standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1228","Pin Configuration — OMTP (legacy standard)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1279","Tip: left channel",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — OMTP (legacy standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1305","Ring 1: right channel",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — OMTP (legacy standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1335","Ring 2: microphone / inline remote",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — OMTP (legacy standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1378","Sleeve: ground",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Pin Configuration — OMTP (legacy standard)"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1401","Compatibility",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1421","CTIA/AHJ is used by Apple, most modern Android devices, and Windows laptops",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1501","OMTP was used by older Nokia phones and some Asian-market handsets",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1572","Plugging a headset wired to one standard into a jack wired to the other still passes left/right audio correctly (tip and ring 1 match), but the microphone does not work, since only the ring 2/sleeve pair is swapped",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1791","Fits into the same jack as Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm and Audio/Connector/Phone/TS/3.5mm plugs, which simply leave the extra ring(s) unconnected",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1953","Common Use Cases",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1976","Smartphone and tablet headsets (earbuds with in-line mic and remote)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Common Use Cases"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-2049","Some cameras and action cams (external mic input, though wiring convention varies by manufacturer)",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Common Use Cases"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-2152","Lavalier/lapel microphones for phones",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Common Use Cases"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-2194","Related References",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-2219","Audio/Connector",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Related References"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-2243","Audio/Connector/Phone/TS/3.5mm",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Related References"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm/","source-block-2282","Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm",["3.5mm TRRS \"Headset Jack\" Audio Connector","Related References"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-60","TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve",[]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-88","Three contacts, two insulating rings. The same plug serves two wirings, and the size and the gear decide which:",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-203","Unbalanced stereo — tip left, ring right, sleeve ground. The usual reading at 3.5 mm.",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve","Three contacts, two insulating rings. The same plug serves two wirings, and the size and the gear decide which:"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-299","Balanced mono — tip and ring carry the two differential halves of one signal, sleeve the shield. The usual reading at 6.35 mm in professional audio.",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve","Three contacts, two insulating rings. The same plug serves two wirings, and the size and the gear decide which:"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-458","A third wiring appears on mixing desks, where one TRS jack is an unbalanced insert point carrying send on the tip and return on the ring.",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-599","Sizes",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-611","Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm — headphones, earbuds, and aux and line cabling.",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve","Sizes"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/","source-block-702","Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/6.35mm — balanced line and insert cabling, and a compact substitute for XLR on small mixing desks.",["TRS — Tip-Ring-Sleeve","Sizes"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-158","3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector",[]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-202","Visual Reference",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-369","Image: public domain (CC0), via Wikimedia Commons",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Visual Reference"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-496","Overview",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-511","TRS stands for Tip-Ring-Sleeve: 3 conductors, 2 insulating rings",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Overview"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-584","At 3.5 mm, TRS almost always carries unbalanced stereo audio — this is the standard headphone/aux plug",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Overview"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-693","At 1/4 in, the same tip/ring/sleeve layout is more often used for balanced mono audio in professional gear; the connotation differs by size and context",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Overview"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-849","Physical Specifications",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-879","Diameter: 3.5 mm (1/8 in)",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-913","Conductors: 3 (tip, ring, sleeve)",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-955","Insulating rings: 2",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-983","Orientation: rotationally symmetric, no keying",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Physical Specifications"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1038","Pin Configuration",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1062","Tip: left channel",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Pin Configuration"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1088","Ring: right channel",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Pin Configuration"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1116","Sleeve: ground",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Pin Configuration"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1139","Common Use Cases",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1162","Stereo headphones and earbuds without a microphone",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Common Use Cases"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1217","Aux/line-in cables between phones, media players, and speakers or car stereos",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Common Use Cases"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1299","Line-level audio breakout on cameras and recorders",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Common Use Cases"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1354","Compatibility",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1374","Physically fits into Audio/Connector/Phone/TRRS/3.5mm jacks; the extra ring on the TRRS jack (mic/ground) is simply left unused",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1510","A Audio/Connector/Phone/TS/3.5mm plug fits into a TRS jack but only drives one channel",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1605","Adapters exist to/from RCA/Connector/Ref/RCA Male pairs for stereo line audio",["3.5mm / 1/8\" Mini Phono TRS Connector","Compatibility"]],["Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/3.5mm/","source-block-1691","An adapter with a 3.5 mm TRS jack and a 6.35 mm TRS plug connects it to Audio/Connector/Phone/TRS/